  "term": "middle temporal gyrus",
  "definition": "The middle temporal gyrus is a brain region; the packet specifically describes its left posterior part as helping with higher-level semantic processing for recognizing objects and integrating visual information. In this study context, it appears to support recognizing shapes and reconstructing them during drawing.",
